1. Variables & ScopeVariables act as containers for storing data values. Modern JavaScript provides three distinct ways to declare variables:const: Block-scoped variable. Cannot be reassigned after declaration. It must be initialized immediately.let: Block-scoped variable. It can be reassigned but not redeclared within the same scope.var: Function-scoped or globally-scoped variable. It can be redeclared and reassigned, but it is prone to scoping bugs. Avoid using this in modern code.
